### MODEL (turn 2)
The bug is in `percentile`: it indexes with `int(p/100 * n)` instead of the nearest-rank index `ceil(p/100 * n) - 1`. I'll fix that, add regression cases for both reported examples, and run the tests.
[tool call luau]
print(edit("logkit/stats.py",
[==[    s = sorted(values)
    return s[min(len(s) - 1, int(p / 100 * len(s)))]]==],
[==[    s = sorted(values)
    rank = math.ceil(p * len(s) / 100)
    return s[min(len(s) - 1, max(0, rank - 1))]]==]))

